# Android HTTP proxy rules

## Scope

- `Settings.Global.HTTP_PROXY`
- `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS` (privileged)
- Save/restore previous proxy value
- Loopback-only listen then write Global

Does **not** cover: Shizuku process (shizuku.mdc), APN editor (forbidden).

## Invariants

1. Enable order: bind 127.0.0.1 → `putString(HTTP_PROXY, "127.0.0.1:$port")`.
2. Disable: restore saved value or `:0`.
3. Force-stop may skip `onDestroy`. Next process start: if runtime ≠ PROXY, `disable()`.
4. No APN `proxy`/`port` writes in v1.
5. PROXY is convenience, not a leak-proof tunnel. Apps may ignore Global (HTTP/3, custom stacks).

## External docs

**Docs (if stuck):** https://developer.android.com/reference/android/provider/Settings.Global#HTTP_PROXY

Permission: `android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS`

- last consulted: 2026-08

## Problem classes

### `Dead proxy after crash`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Browser hangs on all HTTP | Global still points at old port | `onDestroy`/`onTaskRemoved` disable; boot/start clear if not PROXY |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `SecurityException on putString`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Proxy "on" in UI but Global unchanged | No `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS` | Shizuku or ADB grant; listen still; UI "system proxy inactive" |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Stale loopback saved as user proxy`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| PROXY→VPN leaves `http_proxy=127.0.0.1:oldPort` | `enable()` saved leftover `127.0.0.1:oldPort` (previous session) as "user proxy"; `disable()` restored it | Never save/restore `127.0.0.1:*`. `isLoopbackProxy` any port → treat as ours → restore `:0` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `hasPermission false positive`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `hasPermission()` true but `enable()` throws `SecurityException` | `Settings.Global.getString` does not throw without grant; archive try/catch on read always passed | `hasPermission`: no-op `putString(HTTP_PROXY, current)` round-trip; catch `SecurityException` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Stale adb-forwarded port`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `curl: (52) Empty reply from server` in ~2ms through `adb forward` | Proxy rebound a new ephemeral port on restart; adbd accepts the forward then fails to connect, which reads as an instant empty reply | Re-read `adb shell settings get global http_proxy` and re-forward the current port. Boundary: a **10s hang → 502** is ZT-side (see libzt rules), not staleness |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->
